<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n67011" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετάφημι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>speak among</i> persons, whether in addressing one or more
			of them, or as their spokesman, <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> (only 3sg.
			impf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετέφη</span>), c. dat. pl., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇσιν</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δμῳαῖς</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					18.312
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάντεσσι θεοῖσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					19.100
				</span></i>
			: elsewh. <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> always joins it with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς</span>
			or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖσι</span>, whether a single person
			is addressed, as in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.411
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				4.153
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				19.55
			</span></i>, or more than one, as in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				8.132
			</span></i>:—<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετέφη</span> c. acc.
			pers. is f. l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.795
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
